    {
      "title": "Carney says Canada will pursue ‘unique security and economic alliance’ with EU amid US trade spat",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/15/canada-eu-economic-alliance",
      "description": "<p>Prime minister speaks of strengthening Canada’s economic and political ties to Europe at Canada Investment Summit</p><p>Mark Carney said Canada will pursue a “unique security and economic alliance” with Europe as he positions his country as a base to build in the “new global economic order”.</p><p>Speaking to investors, company executives and government ministers at the inaugural Canada Investment Summit on Tuesday, the prime minister pitched Canada as a “safe harbour” and lucrative home for foreign capital as his government looks to reduce its reliance on trade with the United States.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/15/canada-eu-economic-alliance\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-15T19:08:37"
    },
    {
      "title": "EU moves closer to social media ban for under 13s",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/16/eu-social-media-ban-under-13s",
      "description": "<p>Ursula von der Leyen announces draft law to stop apps ‘depriving children of their childhood’</p><p></p><p>The EU will move forward with <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/jul/13/eu-social-media-ban-children-under-13-ursula-von-der-leyen\">plans for an under 13s social media ban</a>, the head of the European Commission has confirmed.</p><p>Ursula von der Leyen said on Wednesday that social media apps were “depriving children of their childhood” and big tech platforms needed to prove the safety of their products.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/16/eu-social-media-ban-under-13s\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-16T14:39:26"
    },
    {
      "title": "European Union invites Canada to become first ever ‘associate member’",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/16/von-der-leyen-mark-carney-canada-eu-first-associate-member",
      "description": "<p>Commission president says EU must ‘urgently reimagine our partnerships’ as she makes unprecedented offer</p><p></p><p>Canada has been invited to become the first “associate member” of the EU by the European Commission president, Ursula von der Leyen.</p><p>In an unprecedented offer, von der Leyen said on Wednesday that the EU and Canada “see the world with the same eyes” through shared democratic values and common approaches to many big issues, from AI to climate breakdown, the Ukraine war and geopolitics.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/16/von-der-leyen-mark-carney-canada-eu-first-associate-member\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-16T13:48:07"
    },
